e519190b3f1e6dff48e6b9c22348898bd3a2882382a681f7dd645ddb5741cc1\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"bee51375872bcc3a6064731c646c8c37c29e0c36d148668b79a3522eddcb2a68\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"actor height 1.68 m 5 foot 6 TV drama married three times character\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_5027a0933d5943e682e902b1"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the clues more carefully. The \"real-life relative plays alongside but unrelated in series\" is the most distinctive clue. Let me think about shows where this is documented. The ScreenRant article about CW stars who are family might help. Let me also consider \"The Fosters,\" \"Good Trouble,\" or possibly a show like \"Nashville\" or \"Empire.\" Actually, let me reconsider — \"character married 3 times, only one child survives\" strongly suggests a soap opera with dramatic deaths. Let me look at the CW stars family article and also search for specific shows.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d17\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_17c947b38cf94de486879e57","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Empire TV series cast real life relatives character married three times\", \"Nashville TV series cast real life relatives character married children died\", \"Power TV series cast real life relatives character married three times height\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_d6b8c90cb33a484f95510913","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d17\",\"document_chars\":9101,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"30d6d8bd1feaa16d7480eae3bbb0d0772ddf0a956d9870efc705af2df5ace29e\",\"snapshot\":\"a531c0a6be82cbe578781b28cb207ff02e87008856d5212ec2eab3fae2afe076\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Screen Rant\\nauthor: Joseph Allen\\ndate: 2018-04-13\\n---\\nThe CW's slate of programming is a fascinating one. Many of its shows are actually fairly well-regarded, whether they take place inside of the network's sprawling Arrowverse or not. Part of the reason these shows have been so successful is because of their excellent casting and captivating stars.\\n\\nAlthough the CW has a number of great shows on the air and a really great talent pool, they more than occasionally like to cast actors who are actually related to one another in real life, or are married and have decided to form a new family with one another.\\n\\nWhether these two relatives show up on the same show or not depends on the specifics of the situation, but as many of the couples on this list are married, it's often the case that the two of them met while they were filming together. Other times, the relationship between the two actors was the reason that one of them was brought onto a show.\\n\\nWhatever the reasons might be, it's clear that the CW has no fears about keeping things close. After all, if one actor from a family works out, who's to say that others won't, too?\\n\\nHere are 15 CW Stars That Only True Fans Know Are Actually Family.\\n\\nStephen And Robbie Amell\\n\\nThis one is among the most readily apparent on this list, in part because Robbie and Stephen Amell share a last name. The cousins have also made homes for themselves on the CW, where they have both played superheroes.\\n\\nStephen has been Oliver Queen on Arrow for several years, and Robbie has played Firestorm on The Flash. Robbie also played a teleporting hero on Tomorrow People, which has been off the air for a few years now.\\n\\nIn addition to sharing an employer, at least sometimes, the two cousins also look quite a bit alike, and are each quite handsome. Of course, there a number of families who have spawned multiple successful actors because, at the end of the day, part of the reason actors are famous is because of their looks, which the Amells have in spades.\\n\\nJared Padalecki And Genevieve Cortese\\n\\nJared Padalecki has had a pretty long and steady career on television, and he's even had the chance to work with his future wife.\\n\\nPadalecki and Genevieve Cortese actually met on the set of Supernatural when Cortese was a recurring guest during the show's fourth season. Cortese played Ruby, a demon who seduces Padalecki's character and causes a rift to form between Sam and Dean.\\n\\nAlthough the affair between Sam and Ruby proved to be short-lived, Padalecki and Cortese's relationship turned out to be a pretty stable one. The couple eventually got married, and they now live in Austin, Texas with their three children. Supernatural is a show with plenty of tragedy, but things seemed to have ended in a happily ever after for Padalecki and Cortese.\\n\\nAly And AJ Michalka\\n\\nAly and AJ Michalka have been famous since a fairly young age. Both actresses made their debuts on the Disney Channel when they were still quite young, and they also to\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_17c947b38cf94de486879e57"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":false,\"blocks_finish\":true,\"code\":\"read_only_tool_only\",\"executed\":false,\"message\":\"This decision permits only read; no automatic replacement\",\"ok\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_d6b8c90cb33a484f95510913"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the clues. The combination of \"character married 3 times, only one child survives, real-life relative plays alongside but unrelated in series\" is very specific. This sounds like it could be from a telenovela or a show like \"Jane the Virgin\" (which has the real-life relative angle with the Baldoni family). Let me think about \"The Fosters\"/\"Good Trouble\" or possibly \"Queen of the South.\" Actually, let me reconsider — the height clue (1.65-1.70m) and \"real-life relative\" makes me think of specific actors. Let me search for shows where a real-life relative plays an unrelated character.","role":"assistant","tool_cal